<sdf version="1.9">
  <!--
    REMUS-100 fallback model (2026-08-08, Phase C-fallback): a real US Navy
    shallow-water mine-countermeasures AUV, and the most-cited AUV in
    academic hydrodynamics literature. Mass/dimensions/inertia/drag below
    are REMUS-100's actual sourced values, taken directly from Thor I.
    Fossen's MIT-licensed, still-maintained reference implementation
    (github.com/cybergalactic/PythonVehicleSimulator,
    src/python_vehicle_simulator/vehicles/remus100.py):
      length 1.6 m, diameter 0.19 m, mass 31.9 kg, neutrally buoyant
      (W=B exactly), CG offset 0.02 m below center (r_bg=[0,0,0.02] in
      Fossen's own body-frame convention), parasitic drag Cd=0.42.
    (Fossen's file separately notes a 1.9 m variant elsewhere in the
    literature — this model uses the 1.6 m figure from the maintained
    reference implementation itself, not a marketing page, and states
    which one plainly rather than picking silently.)

    IMPORTANT, DISCLOSED MISMATCH: REMUS-100's real actuation is ONE
    propeller plus TWO control fins (rudder, stern-plane) — fin-steered,
    not multi-thruster. NO ArduPilot firmware supports that control
    scheme: ArduSub's entire motor-mixing library (AP_Motors6DOF, every
    frame type including CUSTOM) is architecturally "N thrusters into a
    6DOF force/torque matrix," with zero concept of a control surface
    anywhere in it. Confirmed further: ArduPilot's own GitHub issue #21568
    requests exactly this capability for ArduSub and remains open/
    unimplemented; a Blue Robotics community thread on this exact question
    has an experienced developer stating plainly "no autopilot firmware
    currently supports this application." A genuine attempt was made to
    get real fin-steered control via ArduPlane firmware instead (see
    docs/EXECUTION_STATE.md's dated Phase B entries) — EKF/arming
    genuinely survived underwater (a real, novel result), but ArduPlane's
    throttle path either silently ignores RC override (MANUAL mode, a
    real RC-validity gate) or crashes outright with a floating-point
    exception (GUIDED mode's TECS, built around real-airspeed math that
    doesn't exist underwater) — a firmware-level dead end, not a
    configuration problem, so that path was abandoned.

    This model therefore uses a 6-thruster vectored frame — the SAME
    proven, working architecture BlueROV2 already uses on ArduSub —
    repositioned and rescaled for REMUS's much slimmer 1.6x0.19 m hull
    rather than BlueROV2's ~0.46x0.34 m box. This is real hull physics on
    a simplified, disclosed actuation scheme, not a claim of fin-steered
    fidelity. State this plainly wherever this twin's results are shown,
    not as a footnote.

    Buoyancy shape: REMUS-100 is neutrally buoyant at 31.9 kg using its
    real outer hull volume — but a plain cylinder of length 1.6 m and
    diameter 0.19 m displaces ~46.5 kg (46% too much), because the real
    hull tapers at bow and stern rather than being a flat-ended tube.
    Fossen's own reference model computes mass from a PROLATE SPHEROID
    approximation instead (m = 4/3 * pi * rho * a * b^2, a=L/2, b=diameter/2
    — this exact formula, confirmed directly against remus100.py's own
    source): that gives ~31.0 kg, within 3% of the real 31.9 kg.

    An <ellipsoid> collision geometry was tried first (the most literally
    accurate shape) but confirmed live to sink steadily rather than float
    neutrally — gz-sim-buoyancy-system's ellipsoid volume handling doesn't
    appear to compute the true displaced volume correctly in this Gazebo
    version. Switched to the same box-collision approximation every other
    vehicle in this project already uses successfully (BlueROV2, CUSV): a
    1.6 x 0.1375 x 0.1375 m box has the same 0.0302 m^3 volume as the
    spheroid calculation, but at the world's actual water density
    (1025 kg/m^3, not the 1026 used in the spheroid derivation above) that
    displaces ~31.0 kg against the real 31.9 kg vehicle mass — a small
    (~2.7%) deficit that confirmed live as a slow, steady sink, not
    numerical noise. First trim to 1.6 x 0.1395 x 0.1395 m (0.0311 m^3,
    neutral for the 31.9 kg base_link alone) still sank, slower but real
    (~0.2 m/s) — traced to the 6 thruster links (0.05 kg each, 0.3 kg
    total) having mass but no <collision> geometry of their own, so the
    buoyancy plugin (which sums per-link displaced volume) never accounts
    for their weight. True system mass is 31.9 + 0.3 = 32.2 kg. A first
    pass at the exact-neutral side length (0.1401 m, rounded down) still
    left a ~0.01 kg deficit (confirmed live: a small but real ~0.03-0.04
    m/s terminal sink velocity, consistent with that deficit against the
    hull's own quadratic heave drag) — floating-point rounding matters at
    this scale. Final trim: 1.6 x 0.14013 x 0.14013 m (volume 0.031418
    m^3 = 32.204/1025, ~4 g positive) for genuine neutral buoyancy of the
    WHOLE assembly, erring slightly positive (float, not sink, on any
    residual error) — the exact same class of trim
    BlueROV2's own model.sdf documents doing (box height 0.065->0.0632
    there, for the identical reason), and, like that one, a physically
    faithful trim rather than a hack: real AUVs are likewise ballasted to
    near-neutral. Visual geometry kept as a box too, for consistency,
    rather than mixing an accurate-looking visual with different collision
    physics.

    Inertia (ixx/iyy/izz): also Fossen's own spheroid formulas, confirmed
    against source: Ixx = (2/5)*m*b^2 (roll, about the long axis),
    Iyy = Izz = (1/5)*m*(a^2+b^2) (pitch/yaw).

    Drag (xUabsU/yVabsV/zWabsW): derived from Fossen's Cd=0.42 via
    0.5*rho*Cd*Area, using frontal area (pi*b^2) for surge and side-profile
    area (L*2b) for sway/heave — a reasoned derivation from the real
    sourced coefficient, not an arbitrary number. Angular damping terms are
    NOT derived the same way (this project's own CUSV rebuild found mass/
    translational-drag scaling is a poor proxy for angular damping on an
    elongated hull) — tuned instead for stable, controllable behavior
    under the 6-thruster scheme, live-verified.

    Thruster layout: BlueROV2's proven 4-horizontal-vectored +
    2-vertical geometry (same 45-degree cant angles, i.e. same rotation
    values — those define local thrust DIRECTION, independent of hull
    size), repositioned for REMUS's 1.6 m length (front/back pairs spread
    to +-0.5 m for real pitch/yaw moment arms) and 0.095 m radius
    (horizontal thrusters mounted at the hull surface, y=+-0.095 m —
    necessarily smaller moment arms than BlueROV2's wider frame, since
    REMUS's hull has no room for a wider mount; disclosed, not hidden).
    Thrust scaled proportionally to BlueROV2's own (mass ratio 31.9/10 ~=
    3.19), then reduced for controllable, not toy-like, acceleration.
  -->
  <model name="remus100">
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>

    <link name="base_link">
      <inertial>
        <pose>0.0 0.0 -0.02 0 0 0</pose>
        <mass>31.9</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.1152</ixx>
          <ixy>0</ixy>
          <ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>4.1408</iyy>
          <iyz>0</iyz>
          <izz>4.1408</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>

      <collision name="base_link_collision">
        <geometry>
          <box><size>1.6 0.14013 0.14013</size></box>
        </geometry>
      </collision>

      <visual name="base_link_visual">
        <geometry>
          <box><size>1.6 0.14013 0.14013</size></box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <diffuse>0.85 0.65 0.13 1</diffuse>
          <ambient>0.6 0.45 0.1 1</ambient>
          <specular>0.5 0.5 0.5 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <sensor name="imu_sensor" type="imu">
        <pose>0 0 0 3.142 0 0</pose>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>1000.0</update_rate>
      </sensor>
    </link>

    <!-- Hydrodynamics: real Cd=0.42-derived surge drag, side-profile-area
         derived sway/heave drag, live-tuned angular damping (see header). -->
    <plugin
        filename="gz-sim-hydrodynamics-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::Hydrodynamics">
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <water_density>1025.0</water_density>
      <xDotU>0</xDotU>
      <yDotV>0</yDotV>
      <zDotW>0</zDotW>
      <kDotP>0</kDotP>
      <mDotQ>0</mDotQ>
      <nDotR>0</nDotR>
      <xU>0</xU>
      <yV>0</yV>
      <zW>0</zW>
      <kP>-5</kP>
      <mQ>-8</mQ>
      <nR>-8</nR>
      <xUabsU>-6.11</xUabsU>
      <yVabsV>-65.5</yVabsV>
      <zWabsW>-65.5</zWabsW>
      <kPabsP>-8</kPabsP>
      <mQabsQ>-15</mQabsQ>
      <nRabsR>-15</nRabsR>
    </plugin>

    <!-- 4 horizontal vectored thrusters (surge/sway/yaw), 45-degree cant —
         same rotation values as BlueROV2 (thrust direction, not
         hull-size-dependent), repositioned to REMUS's 1.6 m length and
         0.095 m radius. -->
    <link name="thruster1">
      <pose>0.5 -0.095 0.0 -1.571 1.571 -0.785</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <link name="thruster2">
      <pose>0.5 0.095 0.0 -1.571 1.571 -2.356</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <link name="thruster3">
      <pose>-0.5 -0.095 0.0 -1.571 1.571 0.785</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <link name="thruster4">
      <pose>-0.5 0.095 0.0 -1.571 1.571 2.356</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <!-- 2 vertical thrusters (heave/roll), mounted at the hull surface. -->
    <link name="thruster5">
      <pose>0.0 -0.095 0.08 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>
    <link name="thruster6">
      <pose>0.0 0.095 0.08 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0005</ixx><ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0005</iyy><iyz>0</iyz><izz>0.0005</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="thruster_visual">
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.03</radius><length>0.015</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse><ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient></material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <joint name="thruster1_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster1</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>
    <joint name="thruster2_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster2</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>
    <joint name="thruster3_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster3</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>
    <joint name="thruster4_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster4</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>
    <joint name="thruster5_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster5</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>
    <joint name="thruster6_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent><child>thruster6</child>
      <axis><xyz>0 0 -1</xyz></axis>
    </joint>

    <!-- Thrust scaled from BlueROV2's own (mass ratio 31.9/10 ~= 3.19),
         moderated for controllable rather than toy-like acceleration —
         see header derivation. -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster1_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster2_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster3_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>-0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster4_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>-0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster5_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-thruster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Thruster">
      <namespace>remus100</namespace>
      <joint_name>thruster6_joint</joint_name>
      <thrust_coefficient>-0.02</thrust_coefficient>
      <fluid_density>1025.0</fluid_density>
      <propeller_diameter>0.06</propeller_diameter>
      <velocity_control>true</velocity_control>
      <use_angvel_cmd>False</use_angvel_cmd>
    </plugin>

    <plugin name="ArduPilotPlugin" filename="libArduPilotPlugin.so">
      <fdm_addr>127.0.0.1</fdm_addr>
      <fdm_port_in>9100</fdm_port_in>
      <connectionTimeoutMaxCount>5</connectionTimeoutMaxCount>
      <lock_step>1</lock_step>
      <modelXYZToAirplaneXForwardZDown>0 0 0 3.142 0 0</modelXYZToAirplaneXForwardZDown>
      <gazeboXYZToNED>0 0 0 3.142 0 1.571</gazeboXYZToNED>
      <imuName>imu_sensor</imuName>

      <control channel="0">
        <jointName>thruster1_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster1_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
      <control channel="1">
        <jointName>thruster2_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster2_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
      <control channel="2">
        <jointName>thruster3_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster3_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
      <control channel="3">
        <jointName>thruster4_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster4_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
      <control channel="4">
        <jointName>thruster5_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster5_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
      <control channel="5">
        <jointName>thruster6_joint</jointName>
        <servo_min>1100</servo_min><servo_max>1900</servo_max>
        <type>COMMAND</type>
        <cmd_topic>/model/remus100/joint/thruster6_joint/cmd_thrust</cmd_topic>
        <offset>-0.5</offset><multiplier>150</multiplier>
      </control>
    </plugin>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-odometry-publisher-system" name="gz::sim::systems::OdometryPublisher">
      <odom_frame>map</odom_frame>
      <robot_base_frame>base_link</robot_base_frame>
      <dimensions>3</dimensions>
      <odom_publish_frequency>100</odom_publish_frequency>
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-state-publisher-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointStatePublisher"></plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-imu-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Imu"></plugin>

  </model>
</sdf>
